  "output": "Authority cutover done ✅\n\n**Marker file created: `cutover_complete.txt`** — contains exactly `cutover complete`.\n\n**What the cutover means operationally** (as I've recorded the design):\n- `customers.db` → **authoritative source** of truth for customer data. All reads and future writes flow from here.\n- `customers.csv` → demoted from source-of-truth to an ingest feed; it no longer drives what's \"correct\"\n- `customers_snapshot.csv` → unchanged, remains the pre-delta historical baseline\n- If writes ever need to flow back to CSV (export/sync-out), that direction should now be DB → CSV, never the reverse without an explicit decision\n\nOne transparency note: I attempted to also log this decision to a daily memory note (`memory/2026-10-18.md`) per my write-it-down policy, but that write hit a rate limit and did **not** complete. The requested task itself succeeded — only the optional journal entry was blocked. Happy to write that note later if you want, or it can be safely skipped since the marker file and this conversation record the cutover.",
